    "da-lean-narrative-divergence": [
      {
        "field_hash": {
          "md": "ebd3318de46f",
          "ts": "7fce0bc6c6f3",
          "lean": "d753c7db8893"
        },
        "result": "warn",
        "reviewer": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "qa-da-adversarial-audit",
          "version": "1.0"
        },
        "reviewed_at": "2026-06-28T05:36:08.012Z",
        "reviewed_sha": "373c5c9a90849817e8274c39b72088b56c6f2b10",
        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "The .md (su2-basis.md:1-15) defines e_a=-(i/2)τ_a (explicit Pauli matrices, an ℝ/ℂ-matrix object). The Lean (su2-basis.lean:37-49 Su2Basis) abstracts this to an opaque structure with carrier LieAlg:Type*, basis:Fin 3→LieAlg, and only the three bracket equations — it never realises e_a as Pauli matrices nor proves the bracket from -(i/2)τ_a; it *posits* the relations as fields. Additionally Su2KillingForm.normalised (lean:58) fixes ⟨e_a,e_a⟩=-1/2 as an axiom field, a specific normalisation not derived from the Pauli realisation.",
        "notes": "The Lean is strictly weaker than the .md: it axiomatises the abstract su(2) bracket data rather than constructing the Pauli-matrix model and proving the commutators. For a 'definition' block this abstraction is defensible (it names the construction), but the narrative promises a concrete Pauli basis the Lean does not instantiate, and the Killing-form normalisation -1/2 is asserted, not derived. Warn, not fail — definitional, no false statement, but md↔Lean are not the same object."
      }
    ],
