        "reviewed_sha": "373c5c9a90849817e8274c39b72088b56c6f2b10",
        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "su2-basis.lean:30-32 introduces R_q = LaurentPolynomial ℤ and q_param/q_inv_param, and Su2KillingForm.killing maps to R_q (lean:56), but the su(2) basis and bracket (md + Su2Basis) carry no q-dependence at all — q is irrelevant to 𝔰𝔲(2)'s real/complex structure constants.",
        "notes": "The base ring R_q=ℤ[q,q^{-1}] is imported for the Killing form (lean:51-60), but 𝔰𝔲(2) structure constants are integers and the Killing-form value -1/2 is rational; pinning the form's codomain to a Laurent-polynomial ring in q is gratuitous (cf. §7c base-ring convention: prefer the weakest ring; no q-deformation is present here). Minor base-ring ambiguity — the q-ring carries no content for this object."
      }
